/* USER CODE BEGIN Header */
/**
  ******************************************************************************
  * @file    app_netxduo.c
  * @brief   NetXDuo applicative file
  *
  *  Architecture change to fix missed metal detections:
  *
  *  BEFORE (broken):
  *    One thread: read sensors → pack → allocate packet → send → relinquish
  *    Problem: network calls block the loop for unpredictable time.
  *             A 2 ms spike during that dead time is never captured.
  *
  *  NOW (fixed):
  *    Thread 1 (AppSensorThread, high priority):
  *      Runs as fast as possible — reads all 32 sensors, runs Detector_Update,
  *      and LATCHES metal_det into a shared result array.
  *      Never blocked by network calls.
  *
  *    Thread 2 (AppUDPThread, lower priority):
  *      Reads the latched results, builds the packet, sends over UDP.
  *      Can block as long as needed without losing any detection events.
  *
  *  Latch behaviour:
  *    is_metal_latch[i] is set to 1 the moment Detector_Update returns true.
  *    It is cleared ONLY after the UDP thread has successfully read it into
  *    the outgoing packet.  This guarantees every metal event appears in at
  *    least one transmitted packet no matter how slow the network is.
  * ******************************************************************************
  */
/* USER CODE END Header */

